course: dictionary
lesson: 9414
title: Squeaky: sounds, voices and phrases
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Squeaky describes a short, high sound, like a squeaky door or a squeaky toy. «Aha! that squeaky board!» cries Toad. The word tells you the floor made a short, high noise, so someone is probably sneaking about.
explain: A squeaky voice is high and thin. Bill, feeble and squeaky, sounds weak as well as high. The words around the word give you the clue: feeble means weak, so squeaky is about how his voice sounds.
explain: Some phrases mean something different from the single word. «Squeaky clean» means very clean, or never doing anything wrong. Check the context: a squeaky clean floor is not making a noise, it is spotless. Swap your meaning into the sentence to see if it still makes sense.
fact: Squeaky is an adjective: squeaky, squeakier, squeakiest.
fact: «Squeaky» means making a short, high sound.
fact: «Squeaky clean» means very clean, or never doing anything wrong.
fact: A squeaky hinge needs oil: the oil makes a slippery layer, so the metal parts slide instead of rubbing.
fact: «Squeaky wheel» is a saying: the person who complains gets attention.
exercise: «Aha! that squeaky board!» cries Toad. What does squeaky mean here? | Very clean | *A short, high sound | Very old | Bright and shiny
exercise: In «Sam tries biscuits, a squeaky ball, even a baby voice», what is squeaky? | *A toy that makes a short, high sound | A ball that bounces very high | A voice that is very deep | A biscuit that is very hard
exercise: What does the phrase «squeaky clean» mean? | *Very clean, or never doing anything wrong | Covered in mud and sticky | Very old and worn out | Making a loud, high noise
test: Why does oil help a squeaky hinge? | It makes the hinge louder | It paints the hinge a new colour | *It makes the parts slide instead of rubbing | It makes the hinge hotter
test: Bill's voice is «feeble and squeaky». What does this tell you? | It is deep and booming | It is very clean | It is quick and cheerful | *It is high, thin and weak
exam: What does the saying «squeaky wheel» mean? | A wheel that never moves | A wheel that is very clean | *The person who complains gets attention | A bicycle that is brand new
